error[Z0111]: `seed` is set once per script, and it is set already
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | seed(2)
  | ^^^^ a second seed
  |
  = help: one seed makes the whole run repeatable; a `seed:` given to one `draw` has a stream of its own

error[Z0111]: `seed` comes after a statement that has already drawn random numbers
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:1
  |
3 | seed(1)
  | ^^^^ too late to set the seed
  |
  = help: put `seed(1)` at the top of the script, before the first draw; the draws so far used the seed 1

error[Z0206]: this gives no value, so it cannot be bound
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:9
  |
1 | let s = seed(1)
  |         ^^^^^^^ its type is Nothing
  |
  = help: `print` and the other statements that print or warn return nothing; use the value they were given

error[Z0401]: `n` of `seed` must be an Int, but this is a Float
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:6
  |
1 | seed(2.5)
  |      ^^^ a Float
  |
  = help: usage: `seed(n)`
